# Step 007 — ADD_CONTRACT SVC_XDUO_0001 WindowLauncher

```step
anchor: ADD_CONTRACT
id: SVC_XDUO_0001
name: WindowLauncher
kind: proxy
language: fsharp
declaring_project: OpticalConstructor.Ui
touches: [OpticalConstructor.Ui, OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests]
depends_on: [3, 5]
```

**How to implement.** Declare in OpticalConstructor.Ui the window-opening seam, generalizing the EditorLaunchers function-record precedent (today at TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:116-141, in Ui after step 3): a WindowKey DU naming every managed window — MaterialsWindowKey, LibraryWindowKey, SolverHandoffWindowKey, CategoryEditorKey, and id-keyed editor keys MaterialEditorKey of MaterialId / SampleEditorKey of SampleId; EntryFreshness = NewUnsaved | Persisted (new entities mint their Guid at Add-window open so the registry keys uniformly by id from the first moment); and the [<ReferenceEquality>] record WindowLauncher of camelCase Result-returning functions that open-or-activate a window for a key (create through an injected per-key window factory when absent, activate the live window when present, re-target an existing Select-state window per step 16), forget a key on close, and decide Select-state modality from the step-5 SelectWindowModality. Provide a mock (stub factories recording calls) plus a mock-driven Ui.Tests test exercising every field through its exact signature.

**Acceptance.** After the step, a mock-driven headless test MUST build a stub WindowLauncher and observe that a second open of the same WindowKey activates instead of creating, two different editor keys create two windows, and every record field is exercised through its exact signature; it passes.
